From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 16:03:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] bpfloader: do not treat the ringbuf test object as critical

bpfRingbufProg.bpf is the only entry in the file list with
critical: true, and it is a test object -- skip_on_user is set, so it is
loaded on userdebug and eng builds only. Its single map is a BPF ringbuf,
which the kernel gained in 5.8, so on 4.9 it cannot load:

  libbpf: map 'test_ringbuf': failed to create: Invalid argument(-22)
  libbpf: failed to load object '/system/etc/bpf/bpfRingbufProg.bpf'
  panicked at system/bpf/loader/bpfloader.rs:736:17

critical: true then does exactly what the comment on that field warns
about. The panic means this loader never reaches its own last step,
execve of netbpfload with "done", which is the only thing that sets
bpf.progs_loaded. Every bpf::waitForProgsLoaded() caller then blocks
forever -- including HealthLoop::UeventInit(), which leaves the health
HAL registered with servicemanager but never polling binder, so
BatteryService.onStart() hangs in IHealth.registerCallback() on
system_server's main thread and the watchdog kills it at 66s.

The other entries that cannot load on this kernel, memevents among them,
already take BPF_FILE_DESC_DEFAULT's critical: false and are merely
logged. Do the same here: a test program should not be able to boot loop
the device.
---
 loader/bpfloader.rs | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/loader/bpfloader.rs b/loader/bpfloader.rs
index f23d882..5834ec8 100644
--- a/loader/bpfloader.rs
+++ b/loader/bpfloader.rs
@@ -330,7 +330,16 @@ const FILE_ARR: &[BpfFileDesc] = &[
     },
     BpfFileDesc {
         filename: "/system/etc/bpf/bpfRingbufProg.bpf",
-        critical: true,
+        // lineage-24.0: not critical. This is a test object (note skip_on_user below) whose only
+        // map is a BPF ringbuf, and BPF ringbufs need kernel 5.8. On the 4.9 kernel this device
+        // ships it cannot load -- "libbpf: map 'test_ringbuf': failed to create: Invalid
+        // argument(-22)" -- and critical: true then does exactly what the comment on that field
+        // warns about: the loader panics, so it never re-execs netbpfload with "done", so
+        // bpf.progs_loaded is never set, so every bpf::waitForProgsLoaded() caller blocks
+        // forever. That wedges the health HAL before it polls binder, BatteryService hangs in
+        // IHealth.registerCallback() on system_server's main thread, and the watchdog kills it.
+        // A test program should not be able to boot loop the device.
+        critical: false,
         skip_on_user: true,
         maps: &[MapDesc::new(GID_ROOT, PERM_GRW, "test_ringbuf")],
         progs: &[ProgDesc::new(GID_ROOT, "skfilter_ringbuf_test")],
